{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:29:23.045Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"34","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed in e1e1c31b, with one half of the prescription declined and the security framing corrected.\n\nWHAT THE EMPTY GENERATION MEANS (checked every producer and consumer first, because rejecting it could have broken legitimate reads):\n- Sole producer: bumpCacheGeneration (cache_entry.go:132) writes cacheGenerationMarker{Generation: cacheTempNameSuffix(rand.Uint64)} - always 32 lowercase hex, never empty. `git log -p --follow internal/sem/cache_entry.go` shows no version ever minted an empty one (feature introduced in 022caa55).\n- Sole consumer: search_cache.go:245-263, which compares cached.DerivedFrom == derivedFrom.\n- The empty generation IS a deliberate, load-bearing sentinel - but only for the marker's ABSENCE. readCacheGeneration returns (\"\", nil) on fs.ErrNotExist because that is the pre-generation state, and every artifact derived before the first --force recorded \"\" in DerivedFrom. TestSelectiveCacheServesLegacyGenerationWhenMarkerAbsent locks that, and it PASSES both with and without this change, so nothing legitimate was closed.\n- A marker that EXISTS but decodes to an empty generation is a different state, and one no producer can reach: its existence asserts a rebuild happened while its value says none ever has. That self-contradiction is what this closes.\n\nREPRODUCED. A probe planting a gzip of {} and of {\"generation\":\"\"} at the marker path, after a --force, with a late in-flight derived write: readCacheGeneration =\u003e \"\", err=\u003cnil\u003e in both cases, and loadOrBuildSearchSnapshot returned hit=true resurrected=true - the pre-force selective artifact was served.\n\nFIX. cache_entry.go now returns an error when a present marker decodes to an empty generation, joining the unreadable-marker cases in failing closed. fs.ErrNotExist is untouched.\n\nREGRESSION TEST. TestSelectiveCacheFailsClosedOnEmptyGenerationMarker (internal/sem/cache_generation_marker_test.go), subtests \"no generation member\" and \"empty generation member\". On a compile-clean revert (deleting only the two-line predicate, leaving `return marker.Generation, nil`; `go build ./...` and `go vet ./internal/sem/` both clean) it fails:\n\n    --- FAIL: TestSelectiveCacheFailsClosedOnEmptyGenerationMarker/no_generation_member (2.29s)\n        cache_generation_marker_test.go:281: a marker carrying no generation was accepted, returning \"\"\n    --- FAIL: TestSelectiveCacheFailsClosedOnEmptyGenerationMarker/empty_generation_member (2.43s)\n        cache_generation_marker_test.go:281: a marker carrying no generation was accepted, returning \"\"\n\nWith the predicate restored: `go test ./internal/sem/` =\u003e ok github.com/entireio/entire-graph/internal/sem 256.765s (full package, after merging origin/main forward; go build ./... green post-merge).\n\nTWO PARTS OF THE FINDING REFUTED.\n1. The \"minted token shape\" check was declined. The token is never parsed, only compared for equality with what a derived entry recorded, so any non-empty value already fails that comparison for artifacts minted under a different one; a shape check adds no discrimination and would retire every existing marker the day the mint format changes. Non-empty is the whole necessary predicate, since it is the empty string alone that aliases the legacy sentinel.\n2. \"Defeating the fail-closed invalidation guarantee\" overstates it - this is not an attack path. The same probe shows that simply UNLINKING the marker produces the identical outcome (readCacheGeneration =\u003e \"\", err=\u003cnil\u003e; hit=true resurrected=true), and that path is contractual and must stay open. Anyone able to plant the empty marker can unlink it instead, or write the derived entry outright. What this change closes is a self-contradictory on-disk state, not an adversary.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1P71KRYE0E3T5K4NV2QDQBE","targetId":"01M1P71KS45H5HZKX0HWYGEWAR","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NE8HTT28JGJ7T5MTW7H75J"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
