    "textSnapshot": "Problem: The semantic provider incompletely reads function parameters in languages with multiple clauses (Scala), parameter groups (Dart), or receiver types (Kotlin), causing missing flows, dropped PARAM_TYPE edges, and type misidentification. Additionally, selective cache entries are not invalidated when --force rebuilds the parent snapshot, leaving stale results served from derived entries.\nSolution: The parser now reads every parameter clause instead of stopping at the first one, unwraps Dart parameter groups to expose their bindings, and positions-orders return-type candidates to skip receiver types in extension functions and parameter-list types. Cache entries are restructured to nest selective snapshots beneath the complete entry they derive from, enabling --force to discard invalidated views as part of the rebuild. Unicode combining marks in parameter names (common in macOS-decomposed source) are now preserved since they are valid identifier continuations in Python, Rust, Go, and others. Ruby block parameters now carry both spellings (block and \u0026block) for flow detection to match call-site forwarding syntax.",
